WEBVTT

00:00:00.819 --> 00:00:02.212
-Guy?
-Dawn?

00:00:02.386 --> 00:00:03.213
Guy!

00:00:03.387 --> 00:00:04.736
Is it really you?

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:06.129
It's you. You're here.

00:00:06.303 --> 00:00:08.262
BOTH:
You're so old! So are you!

00:00:08.436 --> 00:00:09.872
That's what I said!
[laughing]

00:00:10.046 --> 00:00:11.613
Oh, together again.

00:00:11.787 --> 00:00:13.789
These two were inseparable
when they were young.

00:00:13.963 --> 00:00:15.617
Inseparable.

00:00:15.791 --> 00:00:17.184
Dawn's a girl?

00:00:17.358 --> 00:00:18.533
[both laughing]

00:00:18.707 --> 00:00:20.012
-[gasps]
-[sloths purring]

00:00:20.187 --> 00:00:21.318
Hold on, stop.

00:00:21.492 --> 00:00:22.363
-You accessorize with a sloth?
-[laughing]

00:00:22.537 --> 00:00:23.799
I accessorize with a sloth!

00:00:23.973 --> 00:00:25.017
This is Belt.

00:00:25.192 --> 00:00:27.368
[laughs, sighs]

00:00:27.542 --> 00:00:28.369
DAWN:
Mine's Sash.

00:00:28.543 --> 00:00:30.066
Ooh-la-la.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.024
Oh, oh.
Uh, these-these are the Croods.

00:00:32.199 --> 00:00:33.896
-Hello. -Hey.
-'Sup?

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:36.246
And this... th-- Wait.
Nope, nope.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:37.769
-Uh, yeah. This is Eep.
-[sniffing]

00:00:37.943 --> 00:00:39.858
-You're a girl?
-Yeah.

00:00:40.032 --> 00:00:41.077
A girl...

00:00:41.251 --> 00:00:42.426
friend!

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.472
I've never had
a girlfriend before!

00:00:44.646 --> 00:00:46.256
-Me, either! Me, either!
-Girlfriends!

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:47.953
-Okay, careful. Small bones.
-Girlfriends! Girlfriends!

00:00:48.127 --> 00:00:49.216
-Extra vertebrae.
-[Dawn grunts]

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:50.782
-This is amazing.
-What do we do?

00:00:50.956 --> 00:00:51.914
[high-pitched]:
What do we say to each other?

00:00:52.088 --> 00:00:53.220
What's happening to our voices?

00:00:53.394 --> 00:00:54.003
Why are our voices
getting so high?!

00:00:54.177 --> 00:00:55.222
[both squealing]

00:00:55.396 --> 00:00:57.180
[howling]

00:00:57.354 --> 00:01:00.139
[croaking]

00:01:00.314 --> 00:01:04.187
As our houseguests, you're
welcome to anything you want.

00:01:04.361 --> 00:01:05.188
[laughs]

00:01:05.362 --> 00:01:06.885
I know what I want.

00:01:08.017 --> 00:01:09.410
Uh, except for that.

00:01:09.584 --> 00:01:11.847
-[chuckles]
-But there's so many of 'em.

00:01:12.021 --> 00:01:13.370
Aw, sorry, Grug.

00:01:13.544 --> 00:01:16.112
I'm afraid we have
one house rule here.

00:01:16.286 --> 00:01:18.636
-We don't eat the bananas.
-But they're right here.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:21.726
Anything else, anything at all,
is yours to enjoy.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:24.903
But we don't eat the bananas.
[chuckles]

00:01:25.077 --> 00:01:25.904
Really?

00:01:26.078 --> 00:01:26.992
Huh?

00:01:27.166 --> 00:01:28.298
No bananas?

00:01:28.472 --> 00:01:30.300
-Huh?
-But...

00:01:30.474 --> 00:01:32.215
We won't eat your bananas.

00:01:32.389 --> 00:01:34.391
[chuckles]
It's getting late, so...

00:01:34.565 --> 00:01:36.915
Well, we can just
sleep-pile right here.

00:01:37.089 --> 00:01:39.091
Got it. Solid spot, Dad.

00:01:39.266 --> 00:01:41.790
Look, Phil.
They sleep in a pile.

00:01:41.964 --> 00:01:43.879
-Ooh, fun.
-Nuh-uh.

00:01:44.053 --> 00:01:46.751
Actually, everyone gets
their own rooms.

00:01:46.925 --> 00:01:49.319
[gasps]
We get separate rooms!

00:01:49.493 --> 00:01:51.452
-What's a room?
-What's a separate?

00:01:51.626 --> 00:01:54.455
We Bettermans believe that
privacy promotes individuality.

00:01:54.629 --> 00:01:56.239
Unofficial motto.

00:01:56.413 --> 00:01:59.198
Well, we Croods believe
that the pack sticks together

00:01:59.373 --> 00:02:01.418
no matter wh-- What?

00:02:01.592 --> 00:02:03.202
Tell me about my room,
Mr. Better-dad.

00:02:03.377 --> 00:02:05.204
Well, son, it's right this way.

00:02:05.379 --> 00:02:07.816
It all started with
a tree and an idea.

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:10.166
[sighs]

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:12.473
[Belt sighs happily]

00:02:12.647 --> 00:02:15.476
Wow. What a day.

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:17.521
I never thought
I'd see the Bettermans again.

00:02:17.695 --> 00:02:18.522
Hey, you.

00:02:18.696 --> 00:02:20.045
-Hey.
-Wow.

00:02:20.219 --> 00:02:22.396
Sure beats the view
from any cave I know.

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:24.136
Yeah, I can't believe
this place.

00:02:24.311 --> 00:02:26.661
[sighs]

00:02:26.835 --> 00:02:29.664
Oh, this bed is so comfortable.

00:02:29.838 --> 00:02:30.752
[Belt purrs]

00:02:30.926 --> 00:02:32.710
Oh, nobody's foot in my mouth.

00:02:33.755 --> 00:02:35.147
So much better.

00:02:35.322 --> 00:02:37.541
[chuckles] Yeah.

00:02:37.715 --> 00:02:41.458
So, is-is this
that privacy thing

00:02:41.632 --> 00:02:43.330
you were telling me about?

00:02:43.504 --> 00:02:45.810
Just feels kind of...

00:02:45.984 --> 00:02:47.725
far, you know?

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:49.771
Guy?

00:02:50.859 --> 00:02:51.729
Guy?

00:02:51.903 --> 00:02:53.557
[both snoring]

00:02:53.731 --> 00:02:55.124
Guy?

00:02:56.081 --> 00:02:57.387
[grunts]

00:02:57.561 --> 00:03:00.608
Time to watch
some late-night window.

00:03:00.782 --> 00:03:02.566
-[grunts happily] -Ooh, ooh,
check it out, Douglas.

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:03.741
This guy's my favorite.

00:03:04.829 --> 00:03:06.614
-[chuffs]
-Okay, moommoth.

00:03:06.788 --> 00:03:08.311
What you gonna do now?

00:03:08.485 --> 00:03:10.966
-[growls, squeaks]
-Oh!

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:12.620
[laughs]
What an idiot!

00:03:12.794 --> 00:03:14.622
[snoring]

00:03:15.797 --> 00:03:18.060
[snoring loudly]

00:03:18.234 --> 00:03:20.367
[furniture creaks]

00:03:27.199 --> 00:03:28.853
Ugga?!

00:03:29.854 --> 00:03:31.552
Ugga?

00:03:33.858 --> 00:03:35.033
[snoring]

00:03:35.207 --> 00:03:36.687
-Ugga!
-Kill circle!

00:03:36.861 --> 00:03:39.342
Oh. Hey, honey.

00:03:39.516 --> 00:03:41.388
Yeah, I couldn't sleep, either.

00:03:41.562 --> 00:03:42.998
All these separate rooms.

00:03:43.172 --> 00:03:44.478
Who could live
in a place like this?

00:03:44.652 --> 00:03:46.218
-Well...
-And there's something off

00:03:46.393 --> 00:03:48.177
about that Phil Betterman guy.

00:03:48.351 --> 00:03:51.267
-Like, way off.
-Grug, you know what I think?

00:03:51.441 --> 00:03:53.835
-Maybe we could stay.
-Excuse me?

00:03:54.009 --> 00:03:55.837
You're-you're thinking
about staying here?

00:03:56.011 --> 00:03:57.839
No. I want to be in the wild

00:03:58.013 --> 00:03:59.623
fighting vulture rats
for scraps.

00:03:59.797 --> 00:04:01.016
Of course I want to stay.

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:02.452
-Yeah, but...
-It's nice here.

00:04:02.626 --> 00:04:04.367
-But...
-And you were just worried

00:04:04.541 --> 00:04:08.719
about your daughter leaving,
but the pack is together.

00:04:08.893 --> 00:04:10.155
Sorta.

00:04:10.329 --> 00:04:11.853
If you give this place a chance,

00:04:12.027 --> 00:04:13.158
you might actually like it here.

00:04:13.332 --> 00:04:15.552
[sighs]

00:04:15.726 --> 00:04:17.162
Do I have to like Phil?

00:04:17.336 --> 00:04:19.556
You have to be nice.
No hitting.

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:21.515
Okay.

00:04:21.689 --> 00:04:23.647
But if I have to be alone...

00:04:26.128 --> 00:04:28.652
...I'm gonna be alone with you.

00:04:28.826 --> 00:04:31.307
HOPE:
I mean, can you believe it?

00:04:31.481 --> 00:04:35.137
After all these years, and Guy
shows up on our doorstep.

00:04:35.311 --> 00:04:37.487
And to think
that we were worrying

00:04:37.661 --> 00:04:39.184
about Dawn being alone.

00:04:39.358 --> 00:04:40.751
And now Guy's back.

00:04:40.925 --> 00:04:42.710
It's like fate brought them
back together.

00:04:42.884 --> 00:04:44.538
Like it was meant to be.

00:04:44.712 --> 00:04:46.496
But did you see the way

00:04:46.670 --> 00:04:49.368
that cave girl
was holding Guy's hand?

00:04:49.543 --> 00:04:50.369
Mm.

00:04:50.544 --> 00:04:51.675
You don't think Guy could

00:04:51.849 --> 00:04:54.069
possibly be serious
about that Meep?

00:04:54.243 --> 00:04:55.853
Or "Peep"? Or is it "Eep"?

00:04:56.027 --> 00:04:57.289
"Eep." It's "Eep," right?

00:04:57.464 --> 00:05:01.337
Well, I'm just not sure
Eep fits in here.

00:05:01.511 --> 00:05:03.992
You know?
In fact, none of them do.

00:05:04.166 --> 00:05:08.387
Poor things do seem to struggle
with the concept of walls.

00:05:08.562 --> 00:05:10.999
I don't know if cave people
belong in a modern world.

00:05:11.173 --> 00:05:13.697
[Thunk laughing hysterically]

00:05:13.871 --> 00:05:16.134
I'm gonna watch window forever!

00:05:16.308 --> 00:05:17.875
Do they know that?

00:05:18.049 --> 00:05:20.443
I feel like we just
need to help them understand

00:05:20.617 --> 00:05:22.576
that they have a bright future.

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:24.316
Outside these walls.

00:05:25.317 --> 00:05:26.536
[snorting]

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:29.800
And Guy's future
is inside the walls.

00:05:29.974 --> 00:05:31.672
-With Dawn.
-Dawn.

00:05:31.846 --> 00:05:34.326
Hope Betterman,
always thinking of others.

00:05:34.501 --> 00:05:37.025
Honestly, I just can't help it.

00:05:38.722 --> 00:05:40.768
[crows, squawks]

00:05:43.814 --> 00:05:46.774
-[yawning]: Oh, that was...
-[neck cracking]

00:05:46.948 --> 00:05:49.385
hands down, the best
night's sleep I've gotten in...

00:05:49.559 --> 00:05:50.995
-Morning, Guy!
-Oh!

00:05:51.169 --> 00:05:52.083
Hi, Mr. Betterman.

00:05:52.257 --> 00:05:53.432
Fresh bitter bean juice?

00:05:53.607 --> 00:05:56.131
Uh, thank you?

00:05:56.305 --> 00:05:58.089
-Hi, Guy.
-[gasps] Mrs. Betterman.

00:05:58.263 --> 00:06:00.701
These are for you.
I made them last night.

00:06:03.442 --> 00:06:05.488
Oh, uh, I should wake Eep up.

00:06:05.662 --> 00:06:07.098
You know, it's been, like,
seven hours since I said,

00:06:07.272 --> 00:06:08.404
uh, "Hey."

00:06:08.578 --> 00:06:10.275
That's adorable.

00:06:10.449 --> 00:06:12.539
You know, let's let
that poor Eep sleep.

00:06:12.713 --> 00:06:13.714
She must be exhausted.

00:06:13.888 --> 00:06:16.107
-Nah, I'm sure she's...
-Oh, look!

00:06:16.281 --> 00:06:18.893
Here's Dawn!
What a coincidence.

00:06:19.067 --> 00:06:20.808
Why, Dawn,
whatever are you doing

00:06:20.982 --> 00:06:22.549
on this particular rope bridge

00:06:22.723 --> 00:06:25.247
at this particular
moment in time?

00:06:26.291 --> 00:06:28.250
My morning chores?

00:06:28.424 --> 00:06:30.557
PHIL and HOPE:
Morning chores!

